"created_at": "2026-10-14T18:25:56.097778+00:00", "user_message": "I have two goals: For our new feature launch to be successful, we need to have a conversion rate of over 15% and secure 20 new customers within the first 3 months.", "assistant_message": "Your launch needs to meet **both conditions within the first three months**:\n- A conversion rate **strictly above 15%**.\n- **20 new customers** secured.\n\nThese replace my vague “Campaign effectiveness” framing. I couldn’t prepare the model update, so **your goals are not yet in the model**; nothing has changed.\n\nOne definition matters before comparing the approaches: **15% of whom—website visitors, trial users, qualified leads, or another group?**\n\nGive your estimate\n\nWhy? Assumption-based planning: name the load-bearing assumption, test it, and replace a guessed number with the decision-maker's own judgement where the choice depends on it."}, {"turn_id": "a0697f42-b54a-4914-bef2-791db275eacd", "created_at": "2026-10-14T18:27:18.903696+00:00", "user_message": "We have 6 months to launch our new features from last Friday, and that's when the initial 3-month sales cycle starts.", "assistant_message": "That clarifies the sequence:\n\n- **Launch:** six months from last Friday.\n- **Sales cycle:** the three months immediately after launch.\n- **Success within that cycle:** conversion strictly above **15%** and **20 new customers** secured.\n\nThe timing matters: hiring and campaign preparation happen before launch; the sales targets are assessed afterwards.\n\nI couldn’t prepare the update because the model still uses the provisional “Campaign effectiveness” goal rather than your launch and sales goals. **Nothing has changed in the model.**\n\n- Offer to revise the goal and timing together.\n\nGive your estimate"}, {"turn_id": "be382662-eb8d-4195-b167-502309ef3708", "created_at": "2026-10-14T18:27:56.719835+00:00", "user_message": "Last Friday was the 9th of October.", "assistant_message": "Thanks—**9 October** is the starting date. That puts launch on **9 April the following year**, with the initial sales cycle ending **9 July**.\n\nI withdrew a proposed date because it assumed a year you hadn’t supplied and attached the deadline to “Campaign effectiveness”, not your launch. Nothing has changed in the model; your two sales goals still need to be represented.\n\n**Which year was 9 October?**"}, {"turn_id": "648cbc26-abda-46e8-97b6-8748672f6fee", "created_at": "2026-10-14T18:28:13.859566+00:00", "user_message": "What do you propose my goal be based on the information I've given you?", "assistant_message": "I’d propose this goal:\n\n> **Achieve a conversion rate strictly above 15% and secure at least 20 new customers during the first three months after the new feature launch, with launch due six months after 9 October.**\n\nTreat these as **joint success conditions**—meeting only one would not count as success.\n\nKeep your **£100,000 annual budget** and **maximum 25% of your time** as constraints, rather than goals. Hiring a manager or using AI plus more advertising are alternative ways to pursue the goal.\n\nThe targets and timing come from you; “at least 20” is my interpretation of “secure 20”. This wording is not yet saved in the model.\n\nThe main unresolved definition is conversion: **15% of which group—visitors, trial users, qualified leads, or something else?**\n\nGive your estimate"}], "action_bar": {"v": 1, "state_key": "00e1ef0d2538a53e", "revision": {"graph_hash": "8c278348d17b455e", "run_key": null}, "priority": [{"action_id": "set_goal", "label": "Set target", "icon": "Target", "group": "gap", "press_id": "act:set_goal", "user_line": "Help me set a target for my goal.", "enabled": true, "why_now": "Your goal has no target yet, so no chance of meeting it can be worked out.", "offer_key": "a909a2f346788079"}], "standard": [{"action_id": "review", "label": "Review", "icon": "ListChecks", "group": "review", "press_id": "agent-next-review-decision", "user_line": "R